EXT. ICE-LOCKED RIVER BARGE, ARCTIC - DAWN

A flat iron barge, locked in white. Its hull creaks. Wind blows ice-dust sideways. A tarp stretched between two crates makes a miserable shelter.

Five figures huddle inside it. ASTRID BJORNSDOTTIR-NKEMELU (40s, fur hood, frost-rimmed eyebrows) pours the last of the tea into a tin cup. Next to her, her brother-in-law DMITRI KOWALCZYK-ROSS (50s, giant gloves) feeds a dying camp stove. On the far side, a young couple, TOMAS and ISABELLA VERRIDGE-LIM (20s each, tangled together under one blanket), whisper. At the tarp's mouth, their guide, OKSANA PETRENKO-ABARA (30s, rifle slung, compass in hand), squints at the horizon.

ASTRID
How long?

OKSANA
The ice should break by noon.

DMITRI
It's been noon for three days.

TOMAS
(to Isabella)
You okay?

ISABELLA
I'm fine.

TOMAS
You're shivering.

ISABELLA
So are you.

ASTRID
Dmitri, give her your gloves.

DMITRI
She has gloves.

ASTRID
Not good ones.

Dmitri strips off the enormous gloves and tosses them to Isabella, who catches them against her chest.

ISABELLA
Thank you.

DMITRI
Don't mention it.

OKSANA
(from the tarp mouth)
Quiet. All of you.

A deep crack booms from under the barge. The whole deck shudders. Dmitri curses. Astrid grabs the tin cup before it spills, but Tomas and Isabella, tangled in the blanket, roll toward the gap and Oksana lunges to haul them back from the edge.

OKSANA (CONT'D)
Back! Away from the rail!

TOMAS
What is it?

OKSANA
The river's moving.

DMITRI
Moving? The river's frozen.

OKSANA
Not anymore.

The barge tilts, a slow, enormous lean. They scramble over crates. Ice groans like a living thing. Water, black and glassy, opens in a long line beside the hull.

ASTRID
(shouting)
Everyone to the stern!

They stumble across the tilting deck, Dmitri carrying the stove, Tomas pulling Isabella, Oksana covering the rear. Astrid reaches the stern first and throws a rope to the ice beyond.

Then the barge rights itself with a thunderous slap, and the lean is gone. Ice-dust swirls. The river, free now, carries them forward.

DMITRI
(laughing, breathless)
Noon.

OKSANA
Told you.
